<cherrytree><node name="Welcome" unique_id="1" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1793817878" ts_lastsave="1793817878"><rich_text>Welcome! This is a demo notebook.

The tree on the left holds your notes; each node can have children.
</rich_text></node><node name="Linux" unique_id="7" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1793817878" ts_lastsave="1793817878"><node name="Shell basics" unique_id="2" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1793817878" ts_lastsave="1793817878"><rich_text>
</rich_text><rich_text underline="single">Navigation:</rich_text><rich_text>

1. pwd: print the working directory
2. ls -la: list files, including hidden ones
3. cd ~: go to the home folder


</rich_text><rich_text underline="single">Files:</rich_text><rich_text>
• cp, mv, rm: copy, move, remove
• find . -name "*.md": search by name
• grep -rn "TODO" .: search inside files
• tar -xzf archive.tar.gz: extract an archive


</rich_text><rich_text underline="single">Tips:</rich_text><rich_text>
• Press Tab to complete file and command names.
• Ctrl+R searches the command history.
• Every command has a manual: </rich_text><rich_text style="italic">man</rich_text><rich_text> &lt;command&gt;.
• Chain commands with &amp;&amp; so the next one only runs if the previous one worked.
• </rich_text><rich_text weight="heavy">Permissions</rich_text><rich_text>: chmod +x script.sh makes a script executable.


</rich_text><rich_text underline="single">Links:</rich_text><rich_text>
• </rich_text><rich_text link="webs https://www.giuspen.net/cherrytree/">CherryTree website</rich_text><rich_text>

</rich_text><rich_text weight="heavy">inline code: </rich_text><rich_text family="monospace">ls -la | grep .conf</rich_text><rich_text>
